      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "In the framework of the Politzer approach, the improved electrostatic potential model for estimating enthalpies of sublimation of nitrogen-rich energetic compounds is proposed on the basis of reliable experimental enthalpies of sublimation for 185 compounds. The accuracy of predicted values is estimated to be within ±20kJ/mol. The model was applied to estimate the solid phase enthalpies of formation of some tetrazole-, tetrazine-, furazan-, and furoxan-based energetic compounds."
      },
